      "title": "Qualifying for Social Security disability",
      "narration": "Rosa paid Social Security taxes for twenty years, which earned her work credits. To qualify for Social Security disability insurance she must be insured: generally 40 credits, with 20 earned in the ten years before disability, and fewer for younger workers. She must also meet the program’s definition. Social Security is funded by payroll taxes and administered federally, and its disability benefit is an earned benefit, not welfare. A separate program, Supplemental Security Income, serves disabled people with little work history and limited means. Most exam questions concern the insurance program.",
