      "title": "Workers compensation benefits",
      "narration": "Maryland workers compensation pays medical expenses for the work injury without dollar limits. It pays wage replacement: temporary total disability at two-thirds of the average weekly wage, up to a state maximum, while the worker recovers; temporary partial while working at reduced pay; permanent partial disability on a schedule for lasting impairments; and permanent total disability for the most serious injuries. It funds vocational rehabilitation and pays death benefits to dependents plus funeral expenses. Disputes go to the Maryland Workers’ Compensation Commission. Benefits are tax-free, and private disability policies offset them.",
