      "title": "How private coverage fits",
      "narration": "Think of the three systems as layers. Workers compensation pays first for job injuries, quickly and without fault. Social Security pays for total, long-lasting disability from any cause, after five months and a strict test. Private disability income fills the gaps: injuries off the job, disabilities that are partial or occupation-specific, the five-month wait and the years before Social Security decides. Group plans offset the government benefits; individual policies generally pay in full, with riders that coordinate. A producer who knows the public programs can show exactly which gap each private dollar covers.",
